WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.590
Our new school gate camera came

2
00:00:02.590 --> 00:00:04.630
with the password “admin”.

3
00:00:05.110 --> 00:00:08.590
The installer shrugged: “They all do.”

4
00:00:09.210 --> 00:00:11.810
So anyone who knows that

5
00:00:11.810 --> 00:00:13.210
could look through it.

6
00:00:14.470 --> 00:00:17.150
Today: how attackers take over connected

7
00:00:17.150 --> 00:00:19.730
things, and how you keep yours safe.

8
00:00:21.030 --> 00:00:22.650
Many devices leave the factory

9
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:24.650
with the same password, like

10
00:00:24.650 --> 00:00:26.830
admin or one two three four.

11
00:00:27.460 --> 00:00:29.500
These defaults are in manuals

12
00:00:29.500 --> 00:00:30.740
anyone can find online.

13
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:34.430
If nobody changes it, anyone can get in.

14
00:00:35.630 --> 00:00:38.150
Attackers don't try devices one by one.

15
00:00:38.810 --> 00:00:41.570
Programs scan the internet all day,

16
00:00:41.910 --> 00:00:44.290
knocking on millions of devices and

17
00:00:44.290 --> 00:00:45.630
trying factory passwords.

18
00:00:46.450 --> 00:00:48.210
A new camera can be found within

19
00:00:48.210 --> 00:00:49.470
minutes of going online.

20
00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.480
A taken-over device can be

21
00:00:52.480 --> 00:00:54.120
controlled from far away.

22
00:00:54.880 --> 00:00:57.240
Join thousands of them, and you have a

23
00:00:57.240 --> 00:01:00.460
botnet: an army of hijacked devices.

24
00:01:01.290 --> 00:01:03.490
Their owners usually notice nothing.

25
00:01:04.860 --> 00:01:07.120
In twenty sixteen, the Mirai

26
00:01:07.120 --> 00:01:09.400
botnet did exactly this.

27
00:01:10.140 --> 00:01:13.060
With about sixty factory passwords, it

28
00:01:13.060 --> 00:01:15.220
took over hundreds of thousands of

29
00:01:15.220 --> 00:01:18.040
cameras and routers, then flooded big

30
00:01:18.040 --> 00:01:19.720
websites until they went offline.

31
00:01:21.130 --> 00:01:21.610
Quick check!

32
00:01:22.250 --> 00:01:24.370
How did Mirai get into so

33
00:01:24.370 --> 00:01:25.910
many devices so easily?

34
00:01:27.150 --> 00:01:29.250
Their owners kept the factory passwords.

35
00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:32.640
Mirai used no clever trick,

36
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:34.020
just the defaults.

37
00:01:34.550 --> 00:01:36.470
That's good news: simple

38
00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:38.310
habits stop most attacks.

39
00:01:39.670 --> 00:01:41.410
Here's how to lock a device down.

40
00:01:42.020 --> 00:01:43.400
Change the default password

41
00:01:43.400 --> 00:01:45.180
to a long new one.

42
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:47.580
Turn on updates, which close

43
00:01:47.580 --> 00:01:49.080
the holes attackers use.

44
00:01:49.750 --> 00:01:51.110
Switch off what you don't

45
00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:52.910
use, like remote access.

46
00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:55.830
And put devices on their own

47
00:01:55.830 --> 00:01:58.090
network, like guest Wi-Fi.

48
00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:01.150
What makes a password strong?

49
00:02:01.860 --> 00:02:03.640
Length, not tricks.

50
00:02:04.290 --> 00:02:07.390
Programs try common words, and swaps

51
00:02:07.390 --> 00:02:09.990
like zero for O, almost at once.

52
00:02:10.690 --> 00:02:14.430
Four random words, like river camel

53
00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:18.370
lantern mint, are long and easy to

54
00:02:18.370 --> 00:02:18.630
remember.

55
00:02:19.960 --> 00:02:21.660
A device should also collect

56
00:02:21.660 --> 00:02:23.420
only what its job needs.

57
00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:27.300
A camera that records sound, or a speaker

58
00:02:27.300 --> 00:02:30.380
that's always listening, gathers far more.

59
00:02:31.080 --> 00:02:33.360
Switch off the rest: data that's

60
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:35.120
never collected can never leak.

61
00:02:36.350 --> 00:02:37.090
Your turn.

62
00:02:37.730 --> 00:02:40.010
Our gate camera can also record

63
00:02:40.010 --> 00:02:42.670
sound, but nobody needs it.

64
00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.160
What should the school do?

65
00:02:46.420 --> 00:02:48.500
Switch the sound off: what's

66
00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:50.280
never recorded can never leak.

67
00:02:50.940 --> 00:02:53.120
Remember: change default passwords,

68
00:02:53.700 --> 00:02:56.140
update, switch off what you don't use,

69
00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.580
and collect only what's needed.

70
00:02:59.210 --> 00:03:01.590
Simple habits stop most attacks.

71
00:03:02.980 --> 00:03:06.960
Try it tomorrow: a device check at home.

72
00:03:07.570 --> 00:03:10.230
With an adult, pick one device,

73
00:03:11.090 --> 00:03:12.410
like the Wi-Fi router.

74
00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:15.680
Check that its password was

75
00:03:15.680 --> 00:03:18.660
changed, updates are on, and

76
00:03:18.660 --> 00:03:21.160
nothing is on that nobody uses.

77
00:03:21.870 --> 00:03:25.090
Only check your own family's devices.
